---
description: Apply React Hook Form v7+ standards for form state management, TypeScript integration, Zod validation, performance optimization, and type safety when building forms in Vite + TypeScript web applications
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

Form Setup & Configuration:

- Use `useForm<TFormData>()` with explicit TypeScript generics
- Configure `resolver: zodResolver(schema)` for Zod validation
- Set `mode: 'onBlur'` or `mode: 'onChange'` for validation timing
- Provide `defaultValues` with proper TypeScript types
- Use `criteriaMode: 'all'` to show all validation errors
- Configure `shouldFocusError: true` for better UX
- Set `reValidateMode: 'onChange'` for real-time validation

Schema Definition & Validation:

- Define Zod schemas with `z.object()` for form data
- Use `z.infer<typeof schema>` for TypeScript type inference
- Apply `.min()`, `.max()`, `.email()` for field validation
- Use `.optional()` and `.nullable()` for optional fields
- Implement `.refine()` for custom validation logic
- Create reusable schema components with `.extend()`
- Use `.transform()` for data transformation before validation
- Apply `.default()` for default values in schemas

Field Registration & Management:

- Use `register(name)` with proper field names
- Apply `{ required: true }` for required fields
- Use `Controller` component for complex inputs
- Implement `useFieldArray` for dynamic form arrays
- Apply `useController` for custom field components
- Use `setValue` and `getValues` for programmatic updates
- Implement `watch` for reactive field monitoring
- Use `trigger` for manual validation triggering

Form State & Performance:

- Monitor `formState.isDirty` for unsaved changes
- Use `formState.isValid` for overall form validity
- Check `formState.isSubmitting` for loading states
- Monitor `formState.errors` for field-specific errors
- Use `formState.touchedFields` for user interaction tracking
- Implement `formState.dirtyFields` for changed fields
- Use `subscribe` for custom state subscriptions
- Apply `shouldUnregister: false` for performance optimization

Error Handling & UX:

- Display errors using `formState.errors[fieldName]`
- Show loading states during form submission
- Implement proper error message formatting
- Use `setError` for custom error setting
- Apply `clearErrors` for error cleanup
- Implement `handleSubmit` with error handling
- Use `onSubmit` and `onError` callbacks
- Apply proper accessibility attributes

TypeScript Best Practices:

- Define form data types using Zod schema inference
- Use `FieldPath<TFormData>` for field name types
- Apply `FieldError` type for error handling
- Use `SubmitHandler<TFormData>` for submission handlers
- Implement `UseFormReturn<TFormData>` for hook return types
- Apply `ControllerRenderProps` for Controller components
- Use `UseFieldArrayReturn` for field array types
- Implement strict typing with `strict: true`

Form Submission & Data Handling:

- Use `handleSubmit(onSubmit, onError)` for form submission
- Implement async submission handlers with proper typing
- Use `reset()` with proper data types for form reset
- Apply `resetField()` for individual field reset
- Use `setFocus()` for programmatic focus management
- Implement `getFieldState()` for field-specific state
- Use `unregister()` for dynamic field removal
- Apply proper error boundaries for submission errors

Performance Optimization:

- Use `useCallback` for submission handlers
- Implement `useMemo` for expensive computations
- Apply `React.memo` for form components
- Use `shouldUnregister: false` for better performance
- Implement proper dependency arrays in hooks
- Use `useWatch` sparingly to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- Apply `useFormState` for selective state subscriptions
- Use `useFormContext` for nested form components

Accessibility & Standards:

- Apply proper `aria-describedby` for error messages
- Use `aria-invalid` for invalid field states
- Implement `aria-required` for required fields
- Use proper form labels with `htmlFor` attributes
- Apply `role` attributes for custom form components
- Use `tabIndex` for proper keyboard navigation
- Implement proper focus management with `setFocus`
- Apply `aria-live` for dynamic error announcements
